  "body": "Vendors Say it's got to Go!\r\n\r\nReady for a new owner to love and enjoy - be in by Christmas!\r\n\r\nWhat a great holiday home this would make. Picture this... a morning swim at Orewa Beach, a flat white from your favourite café, and home again in minutes, to your sunny brick home with a white picket fence and a lawn big enough for whatever life throws at it.\r\n\r\nSet on a generous, sun-drenched corner site, this immaculate home is vacant, beautifully presented and ready for you to simply move in. Orewa's golden beach is just a short stroll away, along with the village shops, cafés and public transport. Leave the car at home and enjoy the coastal lifestyle every day, from your morning swim to a leisurely weekend brunch.\r\n\r\nInside, an approved garage conversion with its own external access gives you genuine flexibility. Use it as a third bedroom, a second living area, a home office or a guest retreat. It suits boarders, extended family or teenagers who want a space of their own.\r\n\r\nOutside, all-day sun and seamless indoor-outdoor flow lead to a big, private lawn. There is plenty of room for the kids and pets to run, a veggie patch to plant, and secure parking for the boat, caravan or RV. The garden shed takes care of the tools and toys.\r\nBest of all, the home is vacant and ready. With no tenants and no waiting, you can settle quickly and start enjoying beachside living straight away.\r\n\r\nWhatever your next chapter looks like, this home has something to offer. First home buyers will find a rare chance to get a foot on the ladder in one of the Hibiscus Coast's most sought-after beachside suburbs, with room to add value and grow into the space. Investors will appreciate a vacant brick home with flexible accommodation and a large corner site, offering strong appeal to tenants and boarders in a proven coastal location. Downsizers can enjoy low-maintenance brick, a sunny lawn and the café and beach lifestyle on the doorstep, with plenty of room for visiting family and none of the burden of a big house. The appeal is real for many looking to secure a property in the lovely seaside town of Orewa. \r\n\r\nCV $1,050,000\r\nRental appraisal *estimate $675 to $725 per week.\r\n\r\nCome and see for yourself, but be quick! Call Rosalind at 0212431153\r\n\r\n***********\r\nDisclaimer: While every effort has been made to ensure the accuracy of these particulars, no warranty is given by the vendor or the agent as to their accuracy. Interested parties should not rely on these particulars as representations of fact but must satisfy themselves by inspection or otherwise. Although high standards have been used in preparing this document, no legal responsibility can be accepted for any loss or damage resulting from the content or use of this information. Any photographs show only certain parts of the property as they appeared when taken, and some photographs may have been digitally enhanced for marketing purposes. Areas, amounts, measurements, distances, and all other numerical information are approximate only.\r\n\r\nNote: Every care has been taken to verify the accuracy of the details in this advertisement. However, its accuracy cannot be guaranteed. Prospective purchasers are requested to take necessary action to satisfy themselves with any pertinent matters.",
